From spencer.graves at PDF.COM  Fri Aug  1 10:51:36 2003
From: spencer.graves at PDF.COM (Spencer Graves)
Date: Fri, 01 Aug 2003 03:51:36 -0700
Subject: Re: subscripts error
References: <000e01c35817$212d60e0$dc25410a@ACNIELSEN.IT>
Message-ID: <3F2A4638.8050502@pdf.com>

You have a syntax problem:  (1:3 - 2) = -1, 0, 1;  I think you want 
1:(length(x)-2), not 1:length(x)-2.  Also, I think you are taking the 
difference in the wrong order.  Consider the following:

> x <- 1:6
> (x2 <- (x[3:length(x)] - x[1:(length(x) - 2)]))
[1] 2 2 2 2

hope this helps.  spencer graves

