Prof. Ripley is correct.  If we correct the syntax syntax errors, we get 
the difference of lag 2, which is different from the second order 
differences, as witnessed by the following example:

> diff(1:6, 2)
[1] 2 2 2 2
> diff(diff(1:6))
[1] 0 0 0 0

(In my earlier reply to this post, I corrected only the syntax errors.)
hope this helps.  spencer graves

