relationship with x using, "glm", I will still want to produce a picture 
to help explain the relationship to others.  For that one can use "cut" 
possibly with "quantile" to categorize x, then "tapply" to get the mean 
y for each x-category.  Then one can plot the y.mean's vs. the x.mean's 
in each cagegory.

spencer graves

